# Keep SQL migrations LF so their sha256 stays stable across OSes (the
# migration-runner is forward-only and hashes file bytes). Prevents Windows
# autocrlf from flipping them to CRLF and tripping "changed after applied".
*.sql text eol=lf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GENERATED ARTIFACTS — produced by a tool, never hand-edited.
#
# `linguist-generated` collapses them in GitHub diffs, and the Dev MCP's
# pre-commit regression check reads the same declaration to skip them when
# extracting removed symbols. That matters: a symbol removed from a generated
# file is not a regression signal, because if the SOURCE changed the source diff
# already carries it — and if it did not, the file regenerates anyway.
#
# Measured 2026-08-10: a 96-file diff produced ~1,460 search needles and left
# 79% of them unscanned inside the time budget. The bulk came from these files —
# three identical copies of a 1.85 MB OpenAPI document, a 4.4 MB test-result
# dump and a 2.6 MB QA matrix. The check was spending its whole budget on its
# own output.
docs/v3.1/api_docs/openapi.json      linguist-generated
docs/v3.1/api_docs/sdk-catalog*.json linguist-generated
apps/*/public/docs/api/openapi.json      linguist-generated
apps/*/public/docs/api/sdk-catalog*.json linguist-generated
scripts/qa-matrix/qa-apis.json       linguist-generated
mcp-server/dev-test-result.json      linguist-generated
mcp-server/*-test-result.json        linguist-generated
*.tsbuildinfo                        linguist-generated

# Build/ops tooling and generated matrices — not application code, and nothing
# in packages/ or services/ imports from here. Declared per-project rather than
# in the MCP's generic exclusion list, because `scripts/` legitimately holds
# referenced source in other repos and a blanket rule there would hide real
# regressions for them.
scripts/**                           linguist-generated
